WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.586
Real data science questions rarely look like clean
textbook prompts.

00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:09.183
On StackOverflow, users describe messy contexts:
their broken code,

00:00:09.263 --> 00:00:14.191
the error they hit, and concrete input-output
examples of what they want.

00:00:14.271 --> 00:00:17.073
Prior benchmarks strip that richness away.

00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:19.749
At the same time, as models get better,

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:23.043
surface-form scores like BLEU become misleading,

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.405
rewarding text that looks right but does not run.

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:33.060
This motivates a benchmark built from natural
problems and judged by actually executing the code.
